<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Settings applied to every test run in this repository.

  The testing platform reports telemetry through Application Insights, and sends it from a timer thread
  part way through a run rather than at startup. Transmitting builds an HTTP handler and compresses the
  payload, both of which load assemblies for the first time, and a load holds the loader lock for as long
  as it takes.

  FileHandleManager.GetOpenHandles() starts a thread per file handle on the machine, upwards of thirteen
  thousand of them for one call, and every one takes that same lock on its way in. A load that holds it
  for longer than the half second the sweep allows a thread leaves all of those threads to be terminated
  where they wait, and a thread killed while holding the loader lock orphans it: every later library load,
  COM activation and thread start in that process then waits forever. Two dumps of a hung run on
  15/09/2026 had the telemetry transmitter on one thread and the sweep blocked on the rest.

  Opting out removes the transmission, and with it the one long hold that was actually observed. It is set
  here rather than per machine so that every run gets it, build agents included.
-->
<RunSettings>
  <RunConfiguration>
    <EnvironmentVariables>
      <TESTINGPLATFORM_TELEMETRY_OPTOUT>1</TESTINGPLATFORM_TELEMETRY_OPTOUT>
    </EnvironmentVariables>
  </RunConfiguration>
</RunSettings>
